- Before setInterval, add: console.log('outside:', this)
- Inside the callback, add: console.log('inside:', this)

Now, two ways to make this inside the callback refer to your Timer instance:

Option A (simplest): use an arrow function so it captures the surrounding this
setInterval(() => {
  this.count++;
}, 1000);

Option B: bind the callback to the instance
setInterval(function () {
  this.count++;
}.bind(this), 1000);

Pick one, run it, and check whether count increases every second. Which option do you want to go with?

